    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d395">

                <pb facs="0437" n="403" sameAs="frus:frus1897/pg403"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Romero to Mr.
                            Sherman.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexican Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1897-10-09"><hi rendition="#italic">October 9,
                        1897</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge
                    the receipt of your note No. 291, of yesterday, in which, referring to the
                    communication which I made to you in my note of September 30 last, that I had
                    received instructions from the Mexican Government extending the time of the
                    convention of March 1, 1889, in order that the International <pb facs="0438"
                        n="404" xml:id="pg404"/> Water Boundary Commission may be enabled to finish
                    the business which it has still pending, you were pleased to send me the English
                    text of a convention on the subject.</p>
                <p>As this draft is taken word for word from the convention signed and approved by
                    the two Governments on the 6th November, 1896, extending the time of the
                    convention of 1889 one year, I find it acceptable; and, in conformity with the
                    suggestion which you were pleased to make, I inclose you the Spanish text of the
                    convention (proposed), taken likewise, with some immaterial changes of form,
                    from the convention of November 6, 1896.</p>
                <p>As I have received full powers to sign this convention from the Mexican
                    Government, I shall be obliged to you if you will be so good as to inform me
                    when you are ready to sign it.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">M. Romero.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d395-a1.xml" xpointer="d395-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
